WEBVTT

00:04.370 --> 00:06.480
It's all burnt up...

00:07.150 --> 00:10.480
Where am I supposed to go now?

00:11.110 --> 00:13.610
It's all right. You're still alive.

00:17.810 --> 00:21.250
For now, you should eat these ohagi.

00:26.870 --> 00:29.120
I remember it all so clearly...

00:29.120 --> 00:32.010
Like it was yesterday.

01:12.550 --> 01:21.310
TONIKAWA

01:12.550 --> 01:21.310
TONIKAWA

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Channel</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Disc Menu</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Recording List</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Start Menu</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Display</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Sub-Menu</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Channel</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Volume</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.220
<b>Program Guide</b>

02:02.910 --> 02:04.220
Darling...

02:04.580 --> 02:07.600
I think the DVR is broken.

02:04.770 --> 02:10.810
<b>Episode 9      A Summer Day</b>

02:08.740 --> 02:10.240
What makes you say that?

02:10.240 --> 02:13.680
I mean, look, I keep pressing, but...

02:13.680 --> 02:14.860
Can I see that for a sec?

02:14.860 --> 02:15.800
Here.

02:17.050 --> 02:20.360
<i>It's probably just dead batteries.</i>

02:22.620 --> 02:24.400
There we go. It's working.

02:27.270 --> 02:28.370
Darling...

02:28.810 --> 02:31.660
You just thought, "Wow, 
what a dummy," didn't you?

02:31.660 --> 02:34.700
What?! Of course not!

02:34.700 --> 02:35.630
Really?

02:36.290 --> 02:39.540
You didn't think I was pitiful 
for being unable to deal with

02:39.540 --> 02:41.450
something as basic as dead batteries?

02:41.450 --> 02:43.220
I would never!

02:43.220 --> 02:45.390
Really? Well, I guess that's okay, then.

02:48.520 --> 02:51.400
<i>My wife is an amazing person.</i>

02:52.500 --> 02:54.640
<i>She has a real air of mystery around her,</i>

02:54.640 --> 02:56.840
<i>she's a deft hand with most things,</i>

02:56.840 --> 02:59.400
<i>and I've never seen her afraid 
or losing her composure.</i>

03:00.100 --> 03:03.660
<i>Even when there are scary-looking 
customers at the bathhouse sometimes...</i>

03:04.310 --> 03:07.230
We don't serve customers with tattoos here.

03:07.230 --> 03:11.290
If you would still like to enter, 
you'll need to cover it up with this tape.

03:11.290 --> 03:12.920
S-Sure...

03:13.440 --> 03:15.920
<i>I honestly think she's too good for me.</i>

03:16.670 --> 03:21.020
<i>Which is why, occasionally... there are 
moments that I can't help but smile at.</i>

03:21.020 --> 03:23.800
Y'know, I think my phone 
is playing tricks on me.

03:24.120 --> 03:25.430
What tricks?

03:25.430 --> 03:28.280
It says my password is wrong.

03:28.280 --> 03:29.430
Did you forget it?

03:29.430 --> 03:30.850
Of course not!

03:30.850 --> 03:34.690
But you don't have to enter your 
password that often anymore, right?

03:34.980 --> 03:41.130
Most of the time, it goes "dink" and 
automatically fills in your ID and password!

03:41.130 --> 03:45.200
So when it tells me to enter them 
the old-fashioned way all of a sudden...

03:45.600 --> 03:47.190
And I tried hard!

03:47.190 --> 03:52.710
But it keeps saying the password that 
I was so confident about is wrong!

03:53.110 --> 03:56.590
Maybe it was changed by 
some sort of super hacker?!

03:56.590 --> 03:58.560
<i>Well, that's a wild theory!</i>

04:00.790 --> 04:05.850
Tsukasa-chan, you haven't changed the 
password since I set it up for you, right?

04:05.850 --> 04:08.060
Huh? Of course not.

04:08.580 --> 04:09.970
In that case...

04:12.780 --> 04:14.650
There. I got in.

04:14.650 --> 04:19.110
Darling... I'm amazed you remember that 
nonsensical string of characters so easily.

04:19.110 --> 04:21.740
Well, there is actually a meaning behind it.

04:22.080 --> 04:24.430
But I think you should probably change it.

04:24.430 --> 04:26.980
It has to be complicated, 
but something you can remember.

04:29.010 --> 04:30.740
Yeah, that's impossible.

04:31.080 --> 04:34.050
<i>I didn't realize we were 
discussing what's possible.</i>

04:34.050 --> 04:36.570
In that case, should I manage 
your password for you?

04:37.310 --> 04:38.250
Would you?

04:38.770 --> 04:42.760
I see! So this is the "dividing 
the housework" part of marriage!

04:42.760 --> 04:44.760
<i>I don't think so, no.</i>

04:45.250 --> 04:47.660
What did you do before 
we were married, though?

04:47.660 --> 04:51.270
Oh, Tokiko took care of that kind of thing.

04:51.740 --> 04:54.870
She might not look the part, 
but she's a hardcore STEM type.

04:54.870 --> 04:56.800
Really? Wow.

04:56.800 --> 04:59.150
I know Python, too.

04:59.450 --> 05:04.700
Y'know, I think it's really cute how some 
things actually give you trouble, Tsukasa-chan.

05:04.700 --> 05:09.280
You really do think I'm a 
dummy, don't you, darling?

05:09.500 --> 05:12.410
What?! I don't think that at all!

05:12.410 --> 05:14.350
No, you do.

05:14.350 --> 05:17.290
Tsukasa-chan is the kind of girl 
who picks up on these things.

05:17.290 --> 05:18.960
Y'know what this is?

05:18.960 --> 05:23.440
This is genuinely one of those "happy wife,
 happy life" type situations.

05:23.440 --> 05:25.860
That kind of sounds like extortion, but...

05:27.740 --> 05:30.530
How about some cake, then?

05:32.020 --> 05:35.200
Oh, come on! Don't give 
me that exasperated look!

05:35.200 --> 05:37.980
You're trying to cheer me up 
with cake in this day and age?

05:37.980 --> 05:40.440
It's not the old days anymore, darling.

05:41.960 --> 05:44.690
Then... 168 apologems in 
your favorite mobile game?

05:46.810 --> 05:49.220
Okay, that sure is a face.

05:49.220 --> 05:54.160
Darling! I know this was my idea, 
but you don't have to suck up <i>that</i> much!

05:54.160 --> 05:57.640
Maybe try for something 
a little more practical!

05:57.640 --> 05:59.290
S-Sorry...

06:00.540 --> 06:04.770
Well, since it's the best option 
so far, I'll settle for that cake.

06:04.770 --> 06:07.530
And that being the case, 
let's go and pick one out.

06:07.530 --> 06:09.220
O-Okay...

06:09.820 --> 06:13.900
All that aside, though, 
I'm glad you're so reliable, darling.

06:15.360 --> 06:17.310
I am?

06:17.310 --> 06:20.570
Of course! I appreciate you 
always being there to help me.

06:20.570 --> 06:22.610
I see. Well...

06:24.660 --> 06:27.360
This is all the thanks I need.

06:27.360 --> 06:30.380
Honestly... You always want 
to do stuff like this.

06:30.380 --> 06:33.120
Yeah. But when I catch your scent,

06:33.120 --> 06:35.870
it makes me want to do whatever you say.

06:35.870 --> 06:38.870
O-Okay, enough! That tickles...

06:39.370 --> 06:43.130
And that's why you went out for cake, huh?

06:43.130 --> 06:47.770
Yep! My wife really is funny, huh?

06:47.770 --> 06:48.880
Uh-huh...

06:48.880 --> 06:53.560
The only thing I worry about 
is if she's always that funny,

06:53.560 --> 06:57.300
or if it's because she's married to me.

06:57.300 --> 06:59.890
That is the least worrying 
worry I ever heard of.

07:00.280 --> 07:05.210
Still, isn't that a good thing? 
Finding your partner cute, I mean.

07:05.210 --> 07:07.650
And there was one other 
thing I wanted to mention...

07:08.230 --> 07:11.160
The other day, something similar happened.

07:12.450 --> 07:14.960
What do you mean?

07:14.960 --> 07:19.490
<i>Look at me, the girl who listens to this nonsense 
without registering a hint of disdain on her face!</i>

07:19.490 --> 07:20.470
<i>Ain't I great?</i>

07:20.470 --> 07:21.920
Good afternoon!

07:22.540 --> 07:25.170
Oh, Yanagi-sensei!

07:27.410 --> 07:28.320
Help yourself.

07:28.320 --> 07:29.460
Thanks.

07:29.460 --> 07:32.000
So, what brings you by today?

07:33.230 --> 07:35.680
I think... there's gonna be a marriage.

07:37.690 --> 07:38.430
For who?

07:38.430 --> 07:42.310
For me! Me! Your old homeroom 
teacher, Yanagi-chan!

07:42.650 --> 07:45.520
Oh, congratulations!

07:45.520 --> 07:46.820
Congratulations.

07:46.820 --> 07:51.130
It's not purely good news, though.

07:51.130 --> 07:52.270
What do you mean?

07:52.270 --> 07:55.590
Is there something you're worried about 
when it comes to marrying Taniguchi-sensei?

07:56.450 --> 08:00.580
Hang on, how did you know 
it's Taniguchi-sensei?

08:00.910 --> 08:04.060
Actually, you weren't surprised 
at the news at all.

08:04.060 --> 08:06.080
Well, I mean...

08:08.910 --> 08:11.770
<i>We saw you two fooling around in the park!</i>

08:11.770 --> 08:14.040
<i>We already saw something crazy!</i>

08:14.660 --> 08:18.210
When I saw you together at the theme 
park, you seemed to really get along!

08:18.210 --> 08:19.950
I felt the same way.

08:19.950 --> 08:21.350
Oh, is that right?

08:22.200 --> 08:25.450
So, what is it you're worried about?

08:25.450 --> 08:29.900
Putting aside how you were fooling 
around in the park at night...

08:29.900 --> 08:31.860
Y-You saw that, too?!

08:32.460 --> 08:33.360
Nope!

08:33.360 --> 08:35.110
Well, whatever.

08:35.610 --> 08:38.760
Actually, I wanted to ask you...

08:38.760 --> 08:42.370
Yuzaki-kun, was there anything you were 
worried about when it came to marriage?

08:43.340 --> 08:44.350
Worried?

08:45.910 --> 08:47.250
Nothing at all!

08:47.650 --> 08:50.000
<i>He can be terrifyingly airheaded at times.</i>

08:50.470 --> 08:54.080
Well, I expected as much, 
but I guess that confirms it.

08:54.080 --> 08:58.880
I was just a little anxious about whether or not 
I was allowed to marry someone so wonderful!

09:00.090 --> 09:02.690
Are you nervous about 
getting married, Sensei?

09:04.140 --> 09:07.150
The other day, we went out 
for beef bowls on a date.

09:08.440 --> 09:09.270
Beef bowls?

09:09.270 --> 09:14.920
Is it some sort of, "I can't believe we 
had beef bowls on a date!" thing?

09:14.920 --> 09:17.280
Come on, I don't think I'm 
a princess or something.

09:17.300 --> 09:20.030
<b>Order take-out on
 your smart phone.</b>

09:17.300 --> 09:20.030
<b>This is where 
beef bowls get good.</b>

09:17.300 --> 09:20.030
<b>We offer
 double meat.

—Ushinoya</b>

09:17.880 --> 09:20.030
I go there by myself all the time.

09:20.560 --> 09:25.290
I go by myself, order one with 
double meat, and polish it off.

09:25.290 --> 09:30.590
But this time, I was kind of happy and 
anxious about going with the one I love...

09:30.590 --> 09:32.670
<i>She really is a sweetheart.</i>

09:33.220 --> 09:34.770
I mean, isn't that nice?

09:34.770 --> 09:37.760
Having a relationship where 
you can let your guard down.

09:37.760 --> 09:38.930
I think so.

09:39.570 --> 09:43.930
But then, when our bowls came out...

09:46.090 --> 09:49.060
Taniguchi-sensei packed the red 
pickled ginger sky-high on his.

09:49.460 --> 09:52.070
Come to think of it,
I've heard of this before.

09:52.070 --> 09:55.990
I see. And that choice of his made you uneasy.

09:55.990 --> 10:00.040
It's not that! It's not that simple!

10:01.650 --> 10:04.510
I'm sure this comes as a 
surprise, Yanagi-sensei.

10:04.510 --> 10:05.500
Y-Yeah.

10:06.110 --> 10:09.930
I started eating them like this after 
reading about it in a certain manga...

10:09.930 --> 10:13.000
And just like they said in the actual manga,

10:13.000 --> 10:15.050
it's actually not that good.

10:16.150 --> 10:17.450
It's not?!

10:17.450 --> 10:19.030
Then why all the ginger?!

10:19.030 --> 10:22.010
Exactly! I asked that very same question!

10:22.010 --> 10:23.410
And he said...

10:23.410 --> 10:26.540
This... is something you can only 
understand if you experience it.

10:26.540 --> 10:30.810
But I don't want you to eat 
it this way, Yanagi-sensei!

10:30.810 --> 10:35.780
Please, Yanagi-sensei! 
I want you to remain normal!

10:36.510 --> 10:38.620
A real head-scratcher, right?

10:38.620 --> 10:40.280
I-I'd say so.

10:40.560 --> 10:45.670
Which is why I figured... I'd try it, too.

10:45.670 --> 10:48.780
What?! You ate one like that, Yanagi-sensei?!

10:48.780 --> 10:52.040
I did! I crossed that line! 
The next day, by myself.

10:52.040 --> 10:55.880
And when I anxiously took a bite...

10:58.470 --> 11:00.790
It wasn't particularly good.

11:00.790 --> 11:01.730
Well...

11:01.730 --> 11:02.890
That makes sense.

11:02.890 --> 11:07.180
But that's not even the worst part!

11:08.540 --> 11:12.650
It wasn't particularly good, 
and I left the restaurant.

11:13.220 --> 11:14.880
And about two days later,

11:14.880 --> 11:19.360
I started getting an insatiable craving for a
 beef bowl piled sky-high with red ginger!

11:20.840 --> 11:25.990
And that was when I realized: This is 
what Taniguchi-sensei was talking about!

11:25.990 --> 11:27.750
It's a swamp!

11:27.750 --> 11:30.870
A beefy swamp that's impossible 
to escape once you've sunk in!

11:31.630 --> 11:36.130
I used to look at people who packed 
on the red ginger with disdain!

11:36.130 --> 11:38.880
"How could they be so 
ridiculous?!" I'd think!

11:38.880 --> 11:44.890
But... because of him... 
I've learned to forgive them.

11:45.570 --> 11:47.040
What exactly is the problem here?

11:47.040 --> 11:49.050
People can change.

11:49.050 --> 11:51.640
And falling in love can drive that change.

11:52.050 --> 11:54.210
Is that something to be glad about?

11:54.210 --> 11:56.470
I-I think so?

11:56.470 --> 11:58.900
Consider it personal growth.

11:59.390 --> 12:05.480
I never wanted to grow into a person who 
eats a big pile of red ginger on her beef bowl.

12:05.480 --> 12:06.870
Well...

12:06.870 --> 12:08.660
That's understandable.

12:09.040 --> 12:13.110
Did you actually mention 
this to Taniguchi-sensei?

12:13.110 --> 12:16.420
I... I could never tell him!

12:16.920 --> 12:18.350
I mean, think about it!

12:18.350 --> 12:22.320
He fell in love with the version of 
me that didn't pile on red ginger!

12:22.320 --> 12:26.430
There's no way he could love me now that I've
 been pickled by all that redness and ginger!

12:27.260 --> 12:29.010
Er...

12:29.010 --> 12:31.180
Seriously, what even is this?

12:31.610 --> 12:35.780
W-Well, you still have to be honest 
with him about it, right?

12:35.780 --> 12:40.410
If he can't accept you as you are, 
getting married seems...

12:40.410 --> 12:42.070
You're right.

12:42.430 --> 12:46.210
Hey, darling, what kind of 
advice are we giving here?

12:47.920 --> 12:49.150
I understand.

12:49.580 --> 12:51.580
I'll try talking to him.

12:52.270 --> 12:55.830
And I'll ask him if he can accept me as I am!

12:59.340 --> 13:02.590
I hope the two of them can find happiness.

13:03.240 --> 13:04.610
I'll be wishing on the stars for it.

13:04.610 --> 13:08.160
I don't know if the stars will 
know what to do with that wish.

13:08.160 --> 13:12.220
Well, I couldn't really follow what 
she was worried about, to be honest...

13:13.200 --> 13:15.600
But do you wanna hit up a beef bowl place?

13:15.600 --> 13:18.350
I was thinking the same thing.

13:25.660 --> 13:28.240
<i>My wife is cute!</i>

13:29.100 --> 13:30.740
Good morning, Nasa-kun.

13:31.060 --> 13:33.540
<i>It's like every time I see her, 
she's cuter... and kinder...</i>

13:34.000 --> 13:35.830
<i>So interesting, and fun to be around!</i>

13:36.730 --> 13:39.090
<i>I love her more every day!</i>

13:39.090 --> 13:41.380
<i>I can't imagine life without her anymore.</i>

13:41.930 --> 13:47.430
<i>Even eating together is fun. Food tastes 
better, and it goes down so smooth.</i>

13:47.430 --> 13:51.810
<i>Eating... and eating... and eating more!</i>

13:53.810 --> 13:56.060
What the heck kind of number is that?!

13:56.480 --> 13:58.570
A-Are you kidding me?

13:58.570 --> 14:02.070
I used to have total control 
over my body weight.

14:02.670 --> 14:05.800
<i>I know I haven't really been 
paying attention lately,</i>

14:05.800 --> 14:08.640
<i>but did I really balloon 
this much in a few months?!</i>

14:08.640 --> 14:09.990
<i>What could have caused it?</i>

14:09.990 --> 14:13.920
<i>There's no reason I should have gained 
so much weight in such a short time...</i>

14:13.920 --> 14:15.330
<i>Wait, there is!</i>

14:15.330 --> 14:17.220
<i>There clearly is!</i>

14:17.220 --> 14:19.580
Care for seconds, darling?

14:20.030 --> 14:25.090
<i>I-I didn't think a happy marriage 
could bring this kind of trap with it.</i>

14:25.400 --> 14:27.470
<i>B-But what I'm really wondering is...</i>

14:28.290 --> 14:34.050
<i>How is she eating the same 
food and not changing at all?</i>

14:35.720 --> 14:37.710
Tsukasa-chan, Tsukasa-chan...

14:40.850 --> 14:43.360
Wha—N-Nasa-kun?

14:43.660 --> 14:46.860
<i>My wife is shockingly slim!</i>

14:47.170 --> 14:48.240
<i>How?!</i>

14:51.650 --> 14:54.540
Darling... have you put on weight?

14:55.340 --> 14:58.200
Wh-Wh-What are you talking about, Tsukasa-chan?

14:58.200 --> 15:01.160
D-Does it look like I have?

15:01.160 --> 15:04.370
Well, not enough to be visibly noticeable...

15:05.000 --> 15:06.130
But how about it?

15:07.060 --> 15:08.630
Have you put on weight?

15:09.860 --> 15:11.180
Y-Yeah...

15:11.180 --> 15:14.390
I see. This is probably my fault.

15:14.770 --> 15:17.560
You're so cute when you're 
enjoying your food.

15:17.560 --> 15:20.140
I end up making too much.

15:20.140 --> 15:22.760
I-It's not your fault!

15:22.760 --> 15:26.150
I've just been eating too much!
 That's not on you!

15:26.610 --> 15:29.650
Thank you. But I'll be more careful anyway.

15:30.060 --> 15:32.740
Honestly, you don't need 
to let it get you down.

15:32.740 --> 15:34.410
Even if you got a bit fluffy,

15:34.410 --> 15:37.160
I'd still think you're cute!

15:39.870 --> 15:42.130
Wh-What's wrong, darling?

15:42.130 --> 15:44.600
Why are you so distraught over this?

15:44.600 --> 15:49.730
I-I admit that I may have 
let my guard down...

15:49.730 --> 15:51.930
Come on, it's fine! Really!

15:52.220 --> 15:53.680
B-But...

15:54.040 --> 15:57.930
Now that I've realized what has happened, 
it's possible to correct the mistake!

15:58.290 --> 16:01.820
Diet! In the end, it's just 
calorie control and exercise!

16:01.820 --> 16:06.300
If you burn more calories than you 
take in, you can't possibly gain weight!

16:06.770 --> 16:09.070
Which is why, as of today, 
I am going to start exercising!

16:09.980 --> 16:13.320
So he said he was going to start 
running ten kilometers a day.

16:13.930 --> 16:16.400
Is he any good with exercise?

16:16.400 --> 16:18.330
I think he should be.

16:18.330 --> 16:19.890
Really?

16:19.890 --> 16:22.330
He wasn't in any sports clubs or anything,

16:22.330 --> 16:24.460
<b>1st Semester       2nd Semester       Final</b>

16:22.330 --> 16:26.580
but he was trying to maintain all A grades.

16:28.210 --> 16:30.590
It's as you've heard, Tsukasa-chan!

16:30.590 --> 16:34.340
When I was in school, not only 
did I work hard on exercise,

16:34.340 --> 16:38.970
but I did quite a few physical 
jobs before we were reunited,

16:39.620 --> 16:41.850
so ten kilometers should be a piece of cake!

16:41.850 --> 16:44.350
Which is why I'm heading out now!

16:51.610 --> 16:54.030
Well, that was a rather thorough 
setup for a punchline.

16:54.030 --> 16:56.020
Outta shape, huh?

16:56.020 --> 16:58.510
Well, since we're done 
with the morning cleanup,

16:58.510 --> 17:00.870
I think I'll join him.

17:00.870 --> 17:03.120
By all means, go ahead.

17:03.440 --> 17:06.770
<i>D-Damn it! I may have stopped exercising,</i>

17:06.770 --> 17:09.150
<i>and I know I've been doing 
nothing but desk work lately!</i>

17:09.150 --> 17:13.380
<i>And I realize I only ever go for a walk 
when I go out with Tsukasa-chan...</i>

17:13.380 --> 17:16.130
<i>But I didn't think that'd make 
me fall this far out of shape!</i>

17:16.800 --> 17:20.140
<i>Damn it, there's no way I can keep this up...</i>

17:22.610 --> 17:24.140
Tsukasa-chan!

17:26.320 --> 17:27.380
You okay?

17:27.380 --> 17:28.720
F-Fine...

17:29.400 --> 17:34.150
O-Okay, maybe I'll do some chin-ups next.

17:42.600 --> 17:45.020
<i>This... is pretty bad.</i>

17:45.020 --> 17:47.960
N-Need some help, darling?

17:49.620 --> 17:51.170
It's okay!

17:51.580 --> 17:55.050
I have to get... at least a little stronger!

17:55.050 --> 17:57.550
Strong enough to protect you...

17:57.550 --> 18:01.050
As your husband!

18:08.580 --> 18:11.130
I couldn't even manage one.

18:11.130 --> 18:13.040
Oh, it's okay.

18:13.040 --> 18:15.990
But as your husband, shouldn't I...

18:15.990 --> 18:19.700
I saved you when we first met, remember?

18:20.440 --> 18:23.450
I can keep you safe.

18:25.340 --> 18:28.250
But I wanted to say that...

18:29.250 --> 18:30.710
Sorry about that.

18:33.030 --> 18:34.460
It's ready, Tsukasa-chan.

18:34.760 --> 18:38.420
Thanks for making this, darling.

18:38.420 --> 18:40.470
I mean, the only hard part is boiling water.

18:40.470 --> 18:42.770
I still appreciate it.

18:42.770 --> 18:46.720
Nothing beats cold noodles 
during a hot summer.

18:48.480 --> 18:51.260
Damn it! Is this place infested?!

18:51.260 --> 18:53.480
Good lord, am I a bug now?

18:53.480 --> 18:58.900
I did you the favor of dropping 
by since you never invite me.

18:59.790 --> 19:02.780
Don't talk while slurping on noodles!

19:02.780 --> 19:04.420
Now, now...

19:04.420 --> 19:07.830
Thanks for coming by in spite of the heat.

19:07.830 --> 19:11.620
See that? At least your 
husband has some manners.

19:11.970 --> 19:15.910
Would it kill you to show 
the elderly some respect?

19:15.910 --> 19:18.380
In what world do I owe you respect?

19:18.720 --> 19:21.410
And given that it's summer,

19:21.410 --> 19:25.490
would it kill you to get out of the 
house a little and maybe come visit me?

19:26.360 --> 19:29.790
Oh, I know! Camping! I want to go camping!

19:29.790 --> 19:33.510
Since I'm here, you should 
invite me on a camping trip.

19:34.480 --> 19:35.670
Why the heck should I?!

19:35.670 --> 19:38.560
Why? Because it's all the rage these days.

19:38.560 --> 19:41.630
I've fallen down a camp video 
rabbit hole on YouTube.

19:41.630 --> 19:42.910
I don't care!

19:43.220 --> 19:47.500
The thing about camping 
is, it cleanses the heart.

19:47.500 --> 19:50.910
You can heal your exhausted heart 
away from the bustle of the city.

19:51.370 --> 19:54.290
Sipping on coffee while looking 
up at the stars at night...

19:54.290 --> 19:56.720
It's like a trip on the galactic railroad.

19:56.720 --> 20:01.930
You become one with heaven and earth, 
and recover a bit of your true nature.

20:02.200 --> 20:03.760
I doubt this means much to you,

20:03.760 --> 20:07.060
given how much time you spend 
staring at that tiny phone screen,

20:07.060 --> 20:10.660
but that's the kind of experience 
camping offers. Understand?

20:10.660 --> 20:12.580
I still don't care!

20:12.580 --> 20:14.310
Heaven and earth...

20:14.570 --> 20:18.570
Becoming one with heaven and earth?

20:19.020 --> 20:22.060
That sounds really interesting!

20:23.550 --> 20:28.210
I've never gone camping before. 
Is that what it's like?

20:28.210 --> 20:31.390
Of course. It's the ultimate in recuperation.

20:31.390 --> 20:34.140
Whoa, hang on a sec, darling!

20:34.140 --> 20:35.460
You're not serious, are you?

20:35.460 --> 20:38.550
Of course! Let's give it a shot.

20:39.910 --> 20:43.920
So we'll all be going 
camping together next week.

20:43.920 --> 20:46.220
Oh, what fun!

20:46.530 --> 20:49.580
Quit trying to force the issue!

20:49.580 --> 20:52.980
Well, if you're dead set 
against it, that's fine.

20:53.370 --> 20:58.480
But would it really hurt to grant the wish of 
someone who probably has so little time left?

21:00.010 --> 21:03.610
Oh, fine. I'll go camping with you, then.

21:03.610 --> 21:06.410
Really? Yay!

21:06.410 --> 21:07.620
Ugh...

21:08.190 --> 21:10.400
Well, I'll head home for today.

21:10.400 --> 21:14.410
This is for you. Share it 
with your husband, okay?

21:15.370 --> 21:18.880
See you soon, you two!

21:20.670 --> 21:22.640
She really is energetic.

21:22.640 --> 21:23.630
I guess.

21:24.170 --> 21:26.880
What did she give you, anyway?

21:26.880 --> 21:29.390
I'm pretty sure I know without opening it.

21:30.430 --> 21:31.890
It's most likely ohagi.

21:32.940 --> 21:35.890
It's all right. You're still alive.

21:38.310 --> 21:41.400
For now, you should eat these ohagi.

21:49.790 --> 21:53.600
She was really happy to 
get some as a gift once.

21:55.290 --> 21:58.750
<b>Closed for the Day</b>

21:55.290 --> 21:58.750
<b>Sorry!</b>

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

23:25.960 --> 23:27.360
Prep is crucial for camping!

23:27.360 --> 23:29.970
So I've been watching a 
bunch of videos about it!

23:29.970 --> 23:31.660
Don't you have anything better to do?

23:31.660 --> 23:33.740
First, you're supposed to 
go camping on your own!

23:33.740 --> 23:35.880
You've clearly only been watching 
a certain type of video.

23:35.880 --> 23:37.970
Also, actors who don't get much 
work anymore do it a lot.

23:37.970 --> 23:39.980
I didn't need to know that.
